# The League of Arathor (509, Alliance) and The Defilers (510, Horde).
# Built from Forever's quest data (quest pages: reputation per quest and the
# objectives), the world database's exclusive groups and standing gates, the
# quartermasters' lists in Forever's NPC data, the Forever client's item
# table (prices before any standing discount) and the base banners' places
# from Forever's object data. Exalted with either faction is the Legacy
# Challenge "Master of Arathi Basin" (one account-wide Legacy Point).
#
# The Battle for Arathi Basin! (8168/8167/8166/8105, 8171/8170/8169/8120) and
# the one-mark quests (Arathi Basin Resources! 8155/8156/8154/8080/8297, Cut
# Arathor Supply Lines 8162/8161/8160/8123/8299) are each one exclusive group:
# one per character, 200 reputation in any bracket. The guide takes the level
# 55 versions (from level 50, full reputation up to 60) and the Brigadier
# General's and Warbringer's level 59 pair (Claiming Arathi Basin 8395 then
# 8397, Conquering Arathi Basin 8438 then 8442). Below level 50 the tips name
# the bracket versions. The Arathi Resource Crate turn-ins of early Classic
# are gone from Forever's data.
# INGAME: in Classic a quest pays less reputation once you are 6 or more
# levels above it (a fifth at most); a Forever beta report says low quests
# paid in full. Which holds for the bracket quests at level 60?
# Reputation per resources is the Classic figure (10 for every 200, every 150
# on the holiday weekend); Forever has published no battleground reputation
# rates.
# ASSUMED: 3 Marks of Honor for a win and 1 for a loss (Classic flow;
# Forever's data has no per-match reward). In-game check: marks after a game.
# The care package quests Forever added for the Darkspear Islands factions
# (98910-98915) show 10 League of Arathor or Defilers reputation on Forever's
# quest pages; left to the Darkspear Islands guide.

step Refuge Pointe
  only Alliance
  when level>=50
  tip Arathi Basin is a 15 against 15 battle over five bases, from level 20: hold bases to gather resources, and the first team to 2000 wins. Queue at any battlemaster in the capitals or from the battleground screen. In Classic every 200 resources your team gathers pay everyone 10 reputation, so a win pays 100 and a close loss nearly as much; a game also pays 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor for a win, 1 for a loss. The three quests here pay 500 reputation together (200, 200 and 100), once. Forever's Legacy Diplomat perk adds up to 10% to every number in this guide.
  level 50
  accept 8105                          -- Field Marshal Oslight: assault four bases, 200
  accept 8080                          -- Sergeant Maclear: one mark, 200
  accept 8395                          -- Alliance Brigadier General: three marks, 100

step Arathi Basin
  only Alliance
  zone Arathi Basin
  when level>=50
  tip Assaulting a base means clicking its banner until it turns: you need not hold it. Four marks in all: one for Sergeant Maclear, three for the Brigadier General. Forever's PvP gear also costs Marks of Honor along with honor: decide what you want before you hand them in. You can carry at most 30 Arathi Basin marks: hand in or spend them before you reach that.
  interact 180091 quest 8105.1 "Assault the Mine banner"
  interact 180090 quest 8105.2 "Assault the Lumber Mill banner"
  interact 180088 quest 8105.3 "Assault the Blacksmith banner"
  interact 180089 quest 8105.4 "Assault the Farm banner"
  collect 20559 quest 8080.1 @46.2,45.4   -- one Arathi Basin Mark of Honor
  collect 20559 x3 quest 8395.1 @46.2,45.4  -- three more marks

step Back to Refuge Pointe
  only Alliance
  zone Arathi Highlands
  when level>=50
  turnin 8395                          -- hand in the three marks first
  turnin 8080
  turnin 8105

step League of Arathor to Friendly
  only Alliance
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip Neutral to Friendly is 3000 reputation. In Classic a win paid 100 and its 3 marks bring 50 more at the Brigadier General (Claiming Arathi Basin, again and again): about 150 a win, some 20 wins. Forever has not published its battleground rates, so count the games as a rough guide. Below level 50 the quests at Refuge Pointe come in a version for your bracket (from level 20): 200 for assaulting the bases, 200 for one mark, then 100 and 50 per 3 marks at the Brigadier General.
  talk 15351 optional                  -- Alliance Brigadier General: Claiming Arathi Basin again, 50 reputation for 3 marks
  rep 509 Friendly

step Control Four Bases
  only Alliance
  zone Arathi Highlands
  when level>=60
  tip At level 60 and Friendly, Field Marshal Oslight asks your team to hold four bases at the same time: 200 reputation, once. It opens Control Five Bases for Exalted.
  level 60
  accept 8114
  complete 8114 @46.2,45.4 map 1461    -- four bases held at once
  turnin 8114

step League of Arathor to Honored
  only Alliance
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip Friendly to Honored is 6000 reputation, about 40 wins at the Classic rate. Friendly opens the first rewards at Samuel Hawke beside Field Marshal Oslight: the Talisman of Arathor trinket for levels 28, 38, 48 and 58 (72s to 4g12s), and food and bandages that work in Arathi Basin (10s to 20s). He also gives one Arathor care package at Friendly (pick the one for your level): 10 reputation and a bag of battleground food and bandages.
  talk 15127 optional                  -- Samuel Hawke: Friendly rewards
  talk 15351 optional                  -- Alliance Brigadier General: 50 reputation for 3 marks
  rep 509 Honored

step League of Arathor to Revered
  only Alliance
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip Honored to Revered is 12000 reputation, about 80 wins. Honored opens the Highlander's belts in plate, lamellar, chain, mail, leather, lizardhide and cloth for levels 28 to 58 (72s to 8g84s).
  talk 15127 optional                  -- Samuel Hawke: Honored rewards
  talk 15351 optional                  -- Alliance Brigadier General: 50 reputation for 3 marks
  rep 509 Revered

step League of Arathor to Exalted
  only Alliance
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip Revered to Exalted is 21000 reputation, about 140 wins: half of the whole climb. Revered opens the Highlander's boots and greaves for levels 28 to 58 (1g7s to 13g65s), the ones with the run-speed bonus.
  talk 15127 optional                  -- Samuel Hawke: Revered rewards
  talk 15351 optional                  -- Alliance Brigadier General: 50 reputation for 3 marks
  rep 509 Exalted

step Samuel Hawke
  only Alliance
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip Exalted gives the Legacy Point "Master of Arathi Basin" and opens the epics: the level 60 Highlander's shoulders in every armor type (12g33s to 18g50s), Cloak of the Honor Guard (12g14s), Ironbark Staff (55g10s) and Sageclaw (44g24s), both from level 55.
  talk 15127                           -- Samuel Hawke: Exalted rewards

step Control Five Bases
  only Alliance
  zone Arathi Highlands
  when level>=60
  tip At Exalted, Field Marshal Oslight asks your team to hold all five bases at the same time. It pays 200 reputation and the Arathor Battle Tabard, the only way to get it.
  level 60
  accept 8115
  complete 8115 @46.2,45.4 map 1461    -- all five bases held at once
  turnin 8115

